MID_EV30_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_004_m01_001: Yes... This will serve as a place to hold our\nwar councils.
MID_EV30_004_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_081: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_002: This space was intended for the gods of the\nDagdan pantheon.
MID_EV30_004_m01_003: Lavish, isn't it? The gods never were ones to do\nthings halfway.
MID_EV30_004_m01_004: Wow... This is one big round table. Very nice.
MID_EV30_004_m01_005: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_006: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_007: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_010: It is a clever design. It allows all to speak equally,\nwith no one seeming to be at the head of the table.
MID_EV30_004_m01_011: That makes it well suited to our needs as we discuss\nhow best to save the world from Balor.
MID_EV30_004_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_012: <NCA>"Shall we get to business?"
MID_EV30_004_m01_013: Yes. We are gathered today to hear our best hope\nof opposing Balor's infernal forces.
MID_EV30_004_m01_014: But first, I again thank those of you who have\nflocked to our cause.
MID_EV30_004_m01_015: You represent a thin strand of hope for the people\nnot just of Dagda, but the entire world.
MID_EV30_004_m01_016: The root of the trouble, of course, is the appearance\nof the gates to the underworld.
MID_EV30_004_m01_017: Of those, we have already destroyed one to liberate\nthe city of Dagsion.
MID_EV30_004_m01_018: Yet eight gates remain. We cannot claim victory until\nthere are none left standing.
MID_EV30_004_m01_019: The armies of the underworld periodically march\nforth through every open gate.
MID_EV30_004_m01_020: They roam the land, attacking the living with no\nprovocation.
MID_EV30_004_m01_021: And as they claim lives, the souls of those slain are\nadded to Balor's forces.
MID_EV30_004_m01_022: Yes...and with all the towns and villages the enemy\nhas destroyed, that's not a small number.
MID_EV30_004_m01_023: I wish we could do more to protect civilians,\nbut we're stretched too thin.
MID_EV30_004_m01_024: These gates are out of sync with the natural world.\nAt most times, they are as insubstantial as a dream.
MID_EV30_004_m01_025: Yet they do attain solidity and grow more active at\nregular intervals.
MID_EV30_004_m01_026: These are the moments when squadrons of the risen\ndead surge forth from each gate.
MID_EV30_004_m01_027: But the sword is double-edged, for it is also at these\nmoments when they are vulnerable.
MID_EV30_004_m01_028: <NCA>"Are they not vulnerable otherwise?"
MID_EV30_004_m01_029: What is immaterial cannot be struck.
MID_EV30_004_m01_030: More importantly, we have little time with which to\naccomplish our goal.
MID_EV30_004_m01_031: With the next solar eclipse, Balor's power will reach\nits zenith. He will manifest fully.
MID_EV30_004_m01_032: Should that happen, he will be a juggernaut let loose\nupon the world. Its destruction will be certain.
MID_EV30_004_m01_033: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_034: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_004_m01_039: I gather that each gate is guarded by a powerful soul\nthat Balor has snared.
MID_EV30_004_m01_040: That boor Dagda is only the first of his parade of\nwretches. We must not take them lightly.
MID_EV30_004_m01_041: A gate can only be destroyed once its gatekeeper is\neliminated and the barrier around it is broken.
MID_EV30_004_m01_042: We were spared the effort last time because our foe\nhappened to destroy it himself.
MID_EV30_004_m01_043: We cannot expect such good fortune again.
MID_EV30_004_m01_044: <NCA>"Understood."
MID_EV30_004_m01_045: But the simple destruction of the gates to the\nunderworld will not suffice.
MID_EV30_004_m01_046: No, our work will not be done while the gates'\narchitect still draws breath.
MID_EV30_004_m01_047: At the finish, we will need to venture into the\nunderworld and slay Balor himself.
MID_EV30_004_m01_048: He will have hidden himself through the gate in his\nown temple.
MID_EV30_004_m01_068: And so before reaching him, we must destroy all the\nother gates scattered around Dagda.
MID_EV30_004_m01_051: Mind you... Hm.
MID_EV30_004_m01_052: What a roundabout plan.
MID_EV30_004_m01_053: Why not set our sights on Balor? And slay him.
MID_EV30_004_m01_054: 'Tis not so simple. The gates to the underworld are\nlinked in power with Balor's domain.
MID_EV30_004_m01_055: Balor is of a piece with his realm. To weaken him,\nwe must first weaken the underworld.
MID_EV30_004_m01_056: That is best done by destroying the gates, the loci of\nits power here.
MID_EV30_004_m01_057: Oh, so we just need to destroy all the underworld\ngates before the solar eclipse.
MID_EV30_004_m01_069: From there, we go to the temple of Balor, travel to\nthe underworld, and kill the big bastard himself.
MID_EV30_004_m01_059: And that's all it takes to save Dagda. Does that about\nsum it up?
MID_EV30_004_m01_060: That is the long and short of it. I'm glad you absorbed\nmy lesson so well.
MID_EV30_004_m01_061: Well, no matter. We can cross that bridge when\nit burns.
MID_EV30_004_m01_062: Now, then. Those gathered here come from various\nand sundry walks of life.
MID_EV30_004_m01_063: Yet I've no doubt you all hold the same wish in\nyour hearts.
MID_EV30_004_m01_064: Namely, to dethrone Balor and restore this land.
MID_EV30_004_m01_065: Lend me your strength, and it shall be done.
MID_EV30_004_m01_066: We shall set off to destroy the gates as soon as you\nfeel ready.
MID_EV30_004_m01_067: I should mention that survivors have begun to return\nto Dagsion. They may know useful things.
MID_EV30_123_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_123_m01_001: Hmm, that's not quite right.
MID_EV30_123_m01_002: You have been making tentative marks with that\nbrush for some time now, I note.
MID_EV30_123_m01_003: I'm trying to create a banner for us, now that we're\nall together.
MID_EV30_123_m01_004: A seamstress in the city said she'd embroider it for\nme, but I need to come up with a good design.
MID_EV30_123_m01_005: Whoa now! You're quite the artist! Is...that some\nkind of bird?
MID_EV30_123_m01_006: Uh... It's supposed to be a dragon.
MID_EV30_123_m01_007: If you seek an emblem...how about this?
MID_EV30_123_m01_008: This looks like the godmarks hung in the temples.
MID_EV30_123_m01_009: But it's unusually complex. What does it mean?
MID_EV30_123_m01_010: It is the banner of the King of Liberation, said to be\nflown by my ancestors in Fódlan.
MID_EV30_123_m01_011: I like the look of it. Reminds me of flames.
MID_EV30_123_m01_012: Indeed. To my memory, it is in fact called the Crest\nof Flames.
MID_EV30_123_m01_013: Unbelievable. Do they know what they're about?
MID_EV30_123_m01_014: Fortuna, their design... Is that what I think it is?
MID_EV30_123_m01_015: You are not mistaken. A few details are off, but 'tis\nrecognizable enough.
MID_EV30_123_m01_016: They have drawn the Diadem of Entirety, which\nholds special significance for us children.
MID_EV30_123_m01_017: 'Tis a singular mark representing the power of the\nprogenitor god—the very same one that I bear.
MID_EV30_123_m01_018: But what confluence of events could have impressed\nit upon humans?
MID_EV30_123_m01_019: <NCA>"Should we stop them?"
MID_EV30_123_m01_020: The progenitor god could take offense, seeing that\nsymbol on their banner, used in this offhand way...
MID_EV30_123_m01_021: Hmm...
MID_EV30_123_m01_022: No. On further reflection, 'tis fitting.
MID_EV30_123_m01_023: Indeed, no banner may be more suited for those\nwho have assembled to depose Balor.
MID_EV30_123_m01_024: For heroes of many walks of life to come together\nunder this banner for a common purpose...
MID_EV30_123_m01_025: Mere coincidence, or the flow of time at work?\nI find it deeply affecting.
MID_EV30_123_m01_026: 'Tis decided—I approve. By all means, fly this\nemblem as your standard in the battle for liberation.
MID_EV30_123_m01_027: Rally the people around the Crest of Flames and save\nthe land of Dagda!
MID_EV30_110_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_110_m01_001: *gasp*
MID_EV30_110_m01_002: Ah. 'Tis only you.
MID_EV30_110_m01_003: This place is special to me. I come here when I have\nmatters to ponder.
MID_EV30_110_m01_004: <NCA>"You seem distressed."
MID_EV30_110_m01_005: <NCB>"Are you hungry?"
MID_EV30_110_m01_006: <ACA>Hmm. I suppose so. Very well spotted.
MID_EV30_110_m01_007: <ACA>You oft seem dense, but at other times your insight\nis keen. You are a puzzle, to be sure.
MID_EV30_110_m01_008: <ACB>You know, when I feel like this, it does sometimes\nhelp to slather honey atop cheese and eat it.
MID_EV30_110_m01_009: <ACB>A bit of sugar might help to spark a thought or two.
MID_EV30_110_m01_010: 'Twas Balor I came here to ponder.
MID_EV30_110_m01_011: In truth, I had not thought him capable of attaining\nsuch power.
MID_EV30_110_m01_012: Our predicament may be even worse than she\nunderstood, I fear.
MID_EV30_110_m01_013: The schemes his daughters wove around Dagda's\ncauldron were intricate indeed.
MID_EV30_110_m01_014: I am ever more certain that they granted Balor\ngreater power than I can imagine.
MID_EV30_110_m01_015: To fight him may prove more difficult than\nI anticipated.
MID_EV30_110_m01_016: <NCA>"It won't be a problem."
MID_EV30_110_m01_017: <NCB>"Then should we give up?"
MID_EV30_110_m01_018: <ACA>You speak so lightly, with little concern for the\nmatters that weigh on me so.
MID_EV30_110_m01_019: <ACA>I note a shift in attitude from your old self. A side\neffect of the new body, perhaps.
MID_EV30_110_m01_020: <ACA>But there is wisdom in your indifference. Fretting\nover our lot will not improve it.
MID_EV30_110_m01_021: <ACB>Unfortunately, she will not allow me that option.
MID_EV30_110_m01_022: <ACB>Besides, how then would we pass the time? Sit by\nand watch the world rot away?
MID_EV30_110_m01_023: <ACB>No...I see no choice for us in this.
MID_EV30_110_m01_024: <ACB>So we struggle on, so long as our blood is quick.
MID_EV30_110_m01_025: In any event, we can only deal with the immediate\nproblem before taking a longer view.
MID_EV30_110_m01_026: And the solution to that problem rests with you.
MID_EV30_110_m01_027: And the solution to that problem rests with you and\nyour allies.
MID_EV30_110_m01_028: 'Tis a heavy burden to bear, I know. I admire you\nall the more for it.
MID_EV30_110_m01_029: Oh...
MID_EV30_110_m01_030: Enter the underworld and slay Balor where he lurks.\nWhat could be simpler?
MID_EV30_110_m01_031: Alas, 'tis sooner said than done.
MID_EV30_110_m01_032: And maybe not done at all without sacrifice.
MID_EV30_101_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_101_m01_001: Oh. Promised One. What are you doing here?
MID_EV30_101_m01_002: <NCA>"Hard at work, I see."
MID_EV30_101_m01_003: <NCB>"I was inspecting the city."
MID_EV30_101_m01_004: <ACA>Yeah. If Pop were here, he'd say, "Hold a spear every\nday." That's what he always used to tell me.
MID_EV30_101_m01_005: <ACA>I've kept it up since I was real young, so I feel\nrestless if I don't do it.
MID_EV30_101_m01_006: <ACB>The city is looking really good, huh? Finally feels like\nthe old Dagsion again.
MID_EV30_101_m01_007: <ACB>But...Dagda the Great killed most of the people\nwho were living here before, didn't he?
MID_EV30_101_m01_008: Promised One, after you saved me I went back to\nRibeira with my family.
MID_EV30_101_m01_009: I was hoping that Pop would get better.
MID_EV30_101_m01_010: I wanted to take Mom to see the world. But the\nworld now isn't the same place it was then.
MID_EV30_101_m01_011: I went back to Ribeira because I had friends there,\npeople who cared about me.
MID_EV30_101_m01_012: And that's where Pop lost the battle with his\nillness too.
MID_EV30_101_m01_013: So I did what I could to protect the village and\nits people.
MID_EV30_101_m01_014: Then when I heard about a big battle on Alcineus\nSpan, I left Ribeira.
MID_EV30_101_m01_015: <NCA>"You were invaluable then."
MID_EV30_101_m01_016: <NCB>"How is your mother?"
MID_EV30_101_m01_017: <ACA>It was nothing. And I was glad for the chance to\nsee you.
MID_EV30_101_m01_018: <ACA>If I hadn't found you there, I probably would have\nbeen a mess.
MID_EV30_101_m01_019: <ACA>I'm glad to think that I was able to pay you back,\neven if it was just a little bit, for saving me.
MID_EV30_101_m01_020: <ACB>Mom's doing well. She's gotten used to village life.
MID_EV30_101_m01_021: <ACB>It took her a while to learn things like cooking and\nrunning errands in the village, but she's got it now.
MID_EV30_101_m01_022: <ACB>Speaking of Mom, I've been thinking\nabout something.
MID_EV30_101_m01_023: <ACB>I got a letter from her. She's heading to Dagsion\nbecause she thinks she can help here.
MID_EV30_101_m01_024: <ACB>Centurio is with her, so I'm sure she'll be fine,\nbut that's a difficult journey.
MID_EV30_101_m01_025: <ACB>Do you know my mom?
MID_EV30_101_m01_026: <ACB>Guess I shouldn't be too surprised. Seems like you\nknow everything there is to know.
MID_EV30_101_m01_027: Promised One, let's do everything we can to save\nDagda together.
MID_EV30_101_m01_028: We have to bring back a world where everyone\ncan smile and laugh and be themselves again.
MID_EV30_101_m01_029: I don't know how to do that, but I'll give my all to\nfigure it out.
MID_EV30_102_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_102_m01_001: Ah. It is you. Why are you here?
MID_EV30_102_m01_002: <NCA>"I came to check on you."
MID_EV30_102_m01_003: <NCB>"I came to fight."
MID_EV30_102_m01_004: <ACA>Well, I am unoccupied. Merely thinking.
MID_EV30_102_m01_005: <ACB>So you say, but I know that you do not mean it.
MID_EV30_102_m01_006: After you saved me from the depths...
MID_EV30_102_m01_007: I wandered the land of Dagda with those I\ncall friends.
MID_EV30_102_m01_008: The risen dead flooded from the underworld, and my\nblade and I were sated.
MID_EV30_102_m01_009: In the midst of that, when I closed my eyes, it was\nyou I would see...
MID_EV30_102_m01_010: You easily blocked my attack, and I could not\nforget it.
MID_EV30_102_m01_011: And now I find you here, standing before me...
MID_EV30_102_m01_012: You have always intrigued me. Since the moment we\nmet in that glade.
MID_EV30_102_m01_013: Rrgh...
MID_EV30_102_m01_032: 
MID_EV30_102_m01_014: <NCA>"That was sudden."
MID_EV30_102_m01_015: <NCB>"I expected as much."
MID_EV30_102_m01_016: <ACA>That was intended to cleave you in twain.
MID_EV30_102_m01_017: <ACA>Impressive. Your skill comes as no surprise.
MID_EV30_102_m01_018: <ACB>I note that you read my intention. That is not easy.\nYou continue to hold my interest.
MID_EV30_102_m01_019: <ACB>And that is precisely why you are a worthy\nopponent. Let us duel!
MID_EV30_102_m01_020: Hm?
MID_EV30_102_m01_021: That look! Your eyes...
MID_EV30_102_m01_022: It is as if they have consumed all this world holds.
MID_EV30_102_m01_023: Prosperity and decline, life and death, transience\nand tragedy... They have swallowed it all.
MID_EV30_102_m01_024: I see you, and my interest in you has only deepened.
MID_EV30_102_m01_025: Very well. I will postpone our duel.
MID_EV30_102_m01_026: <NCA>"Is something wrong?"
MID_EV30_102_m01_027: Till now, I have taken the measure of my opponents\nby crossing blades.
MID_EV30_102_m01_028: But I feel your depths may be unfathomable.
MID_EV30_102_m01_029: For now, all I can say is that I do not yet know you.
MID_EV30_102_m01_030: I will continue to observe you, Promised One.
MID_EV30_102_m01_031: When we have crushed Balor, I will challenge you\nonce again.
MID_EV30_103_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_103_m01_001: Well met, Promised One. I had hoped to speak\nwith you.
MID_EV30_103_m01_002: <NCA>"Are your people safe?"
MID_EV30_103_m01_003: In truth, no. One of the gates to the underworld\nopened in our lands.
MID_EV30_103_m01_004: Though we are not unique in that respect.
MID_EV30_103_m01_005: Fortunately for Saramis, the gate appeared near\nFort Zanbar.
MID_EV30_103_m01_006: That lies beyond Grania's Waist, making it simple\nto defend against.
MID_EV30_103_m01_007: However, it is significantly more troublesome for\nthe Mosa, our longtime foes.
MID_EV30_103_m01_008: The armies flooding from the underworld gate\nsurged into their lands.
MID_EV30_103_m01_009: It has thrown the Mosa into utter turmoil. Their king\ncame to petition us out of desperation.
MID_EV30_103_m01_010: Our longstanding enmity was quickly cast aside as\nwe forged a peace treaty.
MID_EV30_103_m01_011: It is an opportunity that Saramis could scarcely have\nhoped for ever since our founding.
MID_EV30_103_m01_012: All it took to overturn centuries of mutual loathing\nwas a greater threat.
MID_EV30_103_m01_013: <NCA>"Sad, but true."
MID_EV30_103_m01_014: <NCB>"People just need to talk to each other."
MID_EV30_103_m01_015: <ACA>Yes. We are creatures of irony.
MID_EV30_103_m01_016: <ACB>I had taken you for a hardened realist, so this shift\ninto optimism is a surprise.
MID_EV30_103_m01_017: <ACB>Yet your confidence is not unfounded. It is a better\nbasis to lead from, to be sure.
MID_EV30_103_m01_018: But that is not all I wished to discuss. There is also\nthe question of you, Promised One.
MID_EV30_103_m01_019: As I recall, we first met before I took the throne.
MID_EV30_103_m01_020: Yes, on the road back to Megaira from Troy's shrine.
MID_EV30_103_m01_022: A road that was not far from Cybele, I believe.
MID_EV30_103_m01_021: And our next meeting was in the abandoned temple\nof Yu Phas at Dagsion.
MID_EV30_103_m01_023: I came to realize that I often encountered you in\nplaces tied to my goddess.
MID_EV30_103_m01_024: And so I must ask...are you somehow connected\nwith Yu Phas?
MID_EV30_103_m01_025: <NCA>Say nothing.
MID_EV30_103_m01_026: If you would rather not say, I shall let it lie.
MID_EV30_103_m01_027: But your silence implies that I am not far off\nthe mark.
MID_EV30_103_m01_028: Very well. Knowing this has lifted a weight from\nmy chest.
MID_EV30_103_m01_029: I can go to face Balor without reservation\nor restraint.
MID_EV30_103_m01_030: I think it time that we show Balor how Saramis\nmakes war.
MID_EV30_104_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_104_m01_001: Promised One, do you have a minute to talk?
MID_EV30_104_m01_002: <NCA>"Of course."
MID_EV30_104_m01_003: After the games, I planned to travel the continent\nand take it easy.
MID_EV30_104_m01_004: The drive I'd had since the Cydonia Massacre—\nmy craving for revenge—was gone.
MID_EV30_104_m01_005: Everyone on Mahdel's list was dead, and I'd set\naside my desperate pursuit of Bertrand.
MID_EV30_104_m01_006: I felt that I no longer had any purpose in life.
MID_EV30_104_m01_007: Then Dagda the Great was revived, bringing ruin\nto everything...
MID_EV30_104_m01_008: even killing the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV30_104_m01_009: Which snowballed into a war that enveloped all\nof Dagda, and the underworld below.
MID_EV30_104_m01_010: Now, the chaos and disharmony on this continent are\ntoo serious to ignore.
MID_EV30_104_m01_011: I...doubt you'd consider four years a long time.
MID_EV30_104_m01_012: It's felt like a long time for me, though, waiting to see\nyou again, wanting to talk to you.
MID_EV30_104_m01_013: The last time we met, I was in the middle of doing\nsomething desperate and reckless.
MID_EV30_104_m01_014: I was ready to sacrifice myself, saying it would be a\nfitting death.
MID_EV30_104_m01_015: But the truth is...I wanted to survive.
MID_EV30_104_m01_016: And if my father were alive, he would have told me\nto keep living.
MID_EV30_104_m01_017: By saving me, you made me realize that.
MID_EV30_104_m01_018: That realization is how I've been able to stay strong\neven as the world's gone to hell.
MID_EV30_104_m01_019: You always appeared and saved me when I was in\nthe most terrible danger.
MID_EV30_104_m01_020: Which makes you my—I don't even know the right\nword. Hero? Rescuer?
MID_EV30_104_m01_021: It's hard to do much better than "savior."
MID_EV30_104_m01_022: Well, now it's my turn to save you. I'll watch out for\nyou from now on.
MID_EV30_104_m01_023: <NCA>"I'm counting on it."
MID_EV30_104_m01_024: <NCB>"Don't tire yourself out."
MID_EV30_104_m01_025: <ACA>Hehe. That's exactly what I was hoping to hear.
MID_EV30_104_m01_026: <ACB>I can't exactly take it easy, can I? We're talking about\nsaving the world!
MID_EV30_104_m01_027: Promised One, I do have a favor to ask.
MID_EV30_104_m01_028: For years I kept a seal on Obsidian, but considering\nwhat we're up against, I've decided to release it.
MID_EV30_104_m01_029: In exchange, though...I have to pay a price.
MID_EV30_104_m01_030: I have to expose it to the furthest limits of my soul,\nor it won't show its true power.
MID_EV30_104_m01_031: I know it's reckless, but I'm going to do it, because—\nwell, because we need it.
MID_EV30_104_m01_032: What I ask is that, if Obsidian overtakes my mind,\nyou won't hesitate to kill me.
MID_EV30_104_m01_033: Promise me that, and I can fight without fear.
MID_EV30_104_m01_034: <NCA>"I promise."
MID_EV30_104_m01_035: Thank you. With that, I'm ready.
MID_EV30_104_m01_036: Let's set out soon, Promised One, and restore peace\nto the land of Dagda.
MID_EV30_105_m01: 
