MID_EV30_113_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_113_m01_001: So you're the one who saved the city. I can't thank\nyou enough.
MID_EV30_113_m01_002: Oh. Where are my manners? I am the goddess\nAurora, known as the Navigator's Clarion.
MID_EV30_113_m01_003: <NCA>"You're a goddess?"
MID_EV30_113_m01_004: Hehe. I've been living a normal human life in a\nnormal human village until just recently.
MID_EV30_113_m01_005: I left my temple of my own volition, you see.
MID_EV30_113_m01_006: I had been helping my village withstand the \nunderworld's assaults.
MID_EV30_113_m01_007: But I've returned to the city because I felt there\nmight be a greater duty for me to fulfill here.
MID_EV30_113_m01_008: I heard about the destruction of Dagsion's\nunderworld gate.
MID_EV30_113_m01_009: So I made up my mind to come back to my temple\nand serve as I should serve.
MID_EV30_113_m01_010: That's probably presumptuous of someone who \nabandoned her position.
MID_EV30_113_m01_011: But I hope that as a goddess I can provide support for\nall who need it.
MID_EV30_113_m01_012: <NCA>"I admire that."
MID_EV30_113_m01_013: <NCB>"But why would you..."
MID_EV30_113_m01_014: <ACA>I could say the same of you, the one who saved us.
MID_EV30_113_m01_015: <ACA>Honestly, no one believed it when they heard you\nhad destroyed an underworld gate.
MID_EV30_113_m01_016: <ACA>But look how happy everyone is here.
MID_EV30_113_m01_017: <ACB>My son and his friends are fighting so hard to protect\nthis land.
MID_EV30_113_m01_018: <ACB>So I need to do my best too. I'm sure that's what my\nlate husband would have wanted.
MID_EV30_113_m01_019: <ACB>And you rose up to fight for others, didn't you?
MID_EV30_113_m01_020: The fires of hope are alive in our hearts because\nof you.
MID_EV30_113_m01_021: I'm here because of you. I want to help. After all, I've\nheard a lot about you from my son.
MID_EV30_113_m01_022: He told me a savior clad in white saved him, more\nthan once.
MID_EV30_113_m01_023: He said he wanted to help you whenever you call.
MID_EV30_113_m01_024: <NCA>"You have a good son."
MID_EV30_113_m01_025: Yes, I do. I'm very proud of Cai.
MID_EV30_113_m01_026: He respects you so much, and I can't help but to feel\na sense of familiarity...
MID_EV30_113_m01_027: Hmm... Yes... You're familiar to me...
MID_EV30_113_m01_028: But why is that?
MID_EV30_113_m01_029: I feel as though I've known you for a long, long time.
MID_EV30_113_m01_030: But we've only just met. Who exactly are you?
MID_EV30_113_m01_031: Aurora! I've made contact with some survivors from\nyour temple who had fled.
MID_EV30_113_m01_032: We must plan our next steps right away. Please,\nhurry to the branch temple.
MID_EV30_113_m01_033: Oh my. I'm so sorry, but duty calls.
MID_EV30_113_m01_034: I would like to speak with you again sometime.\nFor now, farewell.
MID_EV30_113_m01_048: Oh my. I'm so sorry, but duty calls.
MID_EV30_113_m01_049: I would like to speak with you again sometime.\nFor now, farewell.
MID_EV30_113_m01_035: Hm! She's a spirited one. I see she grew into a strong\nyoung lady.
MID_EV30_113_m01_036: 'Tis good to see she keeps a rosy outlook, despite\nthese times of hardship.
MID_EV30_113_m01_037: I've watched her from afar since she was a child.\nYou know what that's like.
MID_EV30_113_m01_038: <NCA>"I rarely hear you talk about children."
MID_EV30_113_m01_039: <NCB>"What's your interest in Aurora?"
MID_EV30_113_m01_040: <ACA>Hmph! I'll have you know I cherish the little ones.\nIt's just...
MID_EV30_113_m01_041: <ACA>My nature is not like my brethren's. I can't carry\nanother's child.
MID_EV30_113_m01_042: <ACA>Not even if I wanted offspring. And so there is no\npoint in yearning.
MID_EV30_113_m01_043: <ACB>Hah! As a member of the Dagdan pantheon, I am\nlike a big sister to her.
MID_EV30_113_m01_044: <ACB>While we have stayed at arm's length, I have always\nbeen curious about her.
MID_EV30_113_m01_045: <ACB>She was born from complicated circumstances,\nafter all.
MID_EV30_113_m01_046: I didn't know you had the time for such idle chatter.
MID_EV30_113_m01_047: Now away with you. Balor will not defeat himself.
MID_EV30_008_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_008_m01_063: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_064: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_065: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_066: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_067: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_068: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_001: We are ready to launch our attack on the gate to the\nunderworld. Keep a watchful eye out!
MID_EV30_008_m01_002: That's...not the easiest task when you can't make\nanything out. This fog is impenetrable.
MID_EV30_008_m01_003: We can hardly tell where we're walking.
MID_EV30_008_m01_004: Er...I suppose 'twould help if this red mist weren't\nso suffocating.
MID_EV30_008_m01_061: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_005: <NCA>"What is this?"
MID_EV30_008_m01_006: It's reminiscent of the miasma that chokes\nthe underworld.
MID_EV30_008_m01_007: Another foul emanation from the gate,\nI shouldn't wonder.
MID_EV30_008_m01_008: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_009: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_010: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_011: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_017: Be that as it may, 'twould be wise to proceed\nwith caution.
MID_EV30_008_m01_018: Ah! The air seems to be clearing. But what's this?
MID_EV30_008_m01_019: Impossible! Th-this can't be...
MID_EV30_008_m01_020: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_021: The fine details are off, but I know this place.
MID_EV30_008_m01_022: It must be a replica of the real thing, manifested for\nsome unknown purpose.
MID_EV30_008_m01_023: We stand in the White Canyon Zanado—a Nabatean\nparadise for the progenitor god and her children.
MID_EV30_008_m01_024: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_025: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_026: I feel like I was here a long time ago...
MID_EV30_008_m01_027: It was... It was the paradise world within the picture\nthat Zenzele painted.
MID_EV30_008_m01_028: That's right. That cursed paradise mural in the\ntemple of Aurora.
MID_EV30_008_m01_029: What a strange turn of events. Could our adversary\nthe gatekeeper be responsible?
MID_EV30_008_m01_030: Hold...I spy someone seated in the throne ahead.
MID_EV30_008_m01_031: <NCA>"Are you the guardian of the gate?"
MID_EV30_008_m01_032: Promised One! At long last. It's been so dull here\nwithout you.
MID_EV30_008_m01_033: This man seems fearsome. I do not recognize him,\nbut he carries himself like royalty.
MID_EV30_008_m01_034: I scent strength from him, and no mistake. He is a\nworthy opponent.
MID_EV30_008_m01_035: The armies of the underworld bristle with great\nwarriors, I see.
MID_EV30_008_m01_036: We may never know all that Balor is possessed of.
MID_EV30_008_m01_037: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_038: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_039: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_040: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_041: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_042: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_043: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_044: I'd battled and beaten down so many foes in my\nlife—enough to content me, I thought.
MID_EV30_008_m01_045: But then, staring death in the face, there was\na sudden, searing sense of greed.
MID_EV30_008_m01_046: Why should I have to depart before facing the great\nwarriors of the Heroic Games?
MID_EV30_008_m01_047: Like Dietrich—the swordsman admired even\nby Mars, the Bringer of War.
MID_EV30_008_m01_048: Like Bertrand. A prisoner who'd somehow grown\nstrong enough to beat Gladius.
MID_EV30_008_m01_049: At the end, far from satisfied, all I felt was an aching\nhunger to challenge these fighters.
MID_EV30_008_m01_050: Balor granted my desire—resurrecting me into\nthe youthful, virile man you see before you!
MID_EV30_008_m01_051: My power now exceeds what it was even in the\nprime of my life.
MID_EV30_008_m01_052: Oh, and Promised One, I cannot wait to do glorious\nbattle with you!
MID_EV30_008_m01_053: So you gave yourself over to Balor out of a desire\nfor combat.
MID_EV30_008_m01_054: A warrior's greed for battle is a terrible thing.
MID_EV30_008_m01_055: Ha. I see that you and I are like.
MID_EV30_008_m01_056: Rrgh... Yes, I sense that too, foreigner!
MID_EV30_008_m01_057: A true warrior can recognize the other. Can sense\nthe power flowing through their body!
MID_EV30_008_m01_062: 
MID_EV30_008_m01_058: <NCA>"To battle, then."
MID_EV30_008_m01_059: Yes! No need for more words.
MID_EV30_008_m01_060: Approach me now! Show your strength before Breza!
MID_EV30_009_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV30_009_m01_001: Heh. I fought with all my might—more than I ever\nhad in life!—and I lost.
MID_EV30_009_m01_070: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_071: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_072: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_073: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_074: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_075: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_076: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_077: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_078: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_002: There's that settled. I have no regrets anymore.
MID_EV30_009_m01_003: <NCA>"You're satisfied?"
MID_EV30_009_m01_004: Yes, Promised One. Thank you for giving me this at\nthe end.
MID_EV30_009_m01_005: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_006: He's turning to dust. What does that mean?
MID_EV30_009_m01_007: This didn't happen to the other risen dead.
MID_EV30_009_m01_008: Ah, I see. Someone doesn't like that I conceded.
MID_EV30_009_m01_009: I thought after defeat, the risen dead went back to\nthe underworld to recover. What's happening?
MID_EV30_009_m01_010: Perhaps I'm being sent to Tartarus, that place deeper\nthan the underworld.
MID_EV30_009_m01_011: Or perhaps, now that Balor's abandoned me, I'll just\ncease to exist, body and soul.
MID_EV30_009_m01_012: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_013: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_014: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_015: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_016: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_017: I always sought out the mightiest foes I could find,\nto prove my supremacy.
MID_EV30_009_m01_018: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_019: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_020: It felt like a terrible joke. At that unique time in\nhistory, to be encaged in an atrophied husk!
MID_EV30_009_m01_021: The greatest warriors of the age all gathered in\none place, while I strained to even walk?
MID_EV30_009_m01_022: Why couldn't I have my old strength back?\nA chance to prove myself again?
MID_EV30_009_m01_023: That was when I heard Balor's voice calling\nout to me.
MID_EV30_009_m01_024: He extended his hand, and I didn't hesitate a\nmoment to take it.
MID_EV30_009_m01_025: I wanted so desperately to win. It's strange how\ncontent I feel now that I've lost.
MID_EV30_009_m01_026: My fellow warriors, thank you for the lively clash.\nI pray that you live on...
MID_EV30_009_m01_027: and that you never end up like me.
MID_EV30_009_m01_079: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_080: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_028: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_029: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_030: He was an unexpectedly honorable enemy. Even in\ndefeat, he had grace.
MID_EV30_009_m01_031: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_032: Did he truly throw in his lot with Balor simply to\ntest his strength?
MID_EV30_009_m01_033: I suppose I don't understand the heart of a warrior.
MID_EV30_009_m01_034: There are many people like that in this world. Well...\nmany men like that.
MID_EV30_009_m01_035: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_036: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_069: 
MID_EV30_009_m01_037: <NCA>"And what about you?"
MID_EV30_009_m01_038: I understand him well.
MID_EV30_009_m01_039: Yet I do not see value in strength for its own sake.
MID_EV30_009_m01_040: Oh? That seems unlike you. Explain yourself.
MID_EV30_009_m01_041: I am interested in those whose strength\nsurpasses mine.
MID_EV30_009_m01_042: Were I to become stronger than all others...
MID_EV30_009_m01_043: All that would be left to me is dismal boredom.
MID_EV30_009_m01_044: In a way, I do pity Balor.
MID_EV30_009_m01_045: There exists only one he may challenge whose\nstrength exceeds his own.
MID_EV30_009_m01_046: Only one he can face and exert his might. The one\nwho defeated and sealed him away.
MID_EV30_009_m01_047: 'Tis a rare breed who would express pity for Balor.
MID_EV30_009_m01_048: Seriously, is this all men care about? Who's stronger\nthan who?
MID_EV30_009_m01_049: Doesn't anybody want to talk about anything else?\nI've had about enough.
MID_EV30_009_m01_050: Think on it, though.
MID_EV30_009_m01_051: Can you see Dietrich plowing a field? Comforting a\nchild? Fishing, perhaps?
MID_EV30_009_m01_052: Sure. Why not? I'd love to see Sweetie do\nthose things.
MID_EV30_009_m01_053: I've always wanted to take him out to sea and cast\nour nets together.
MID_EV30_009_m01_054: I try, but I fail to conjure the image.
MID_EV30_009_m01_055: I question, though, if my lust for combat is truly a\npart of me.
MID_EV30_009_m01_056: <NCA>"What do you mean?"
MID_EV30_009_m01_057: My ancestor, Lamine, hunted dragons in Fódlan.
MID_EV30_009_m01_058: One of the dragons she killed is said to have laid a\ncurse on her as it died.
MID_EV30_009_m01_059: The curse was laid not just on her but her bloodline.\nWe thirst for blood and court destruction.
MID_EV30_009_m01_060: This curse has dogged House Lamine for some\ngenerations by now. The family has adapted.
MID_EV30_009_m01_061: Perhaps that is what guards you from the corruption\nbrought by Drake's treasures.
MID_EV30_009_m01_062: Yes, that must be it. Oh, Dietrich. You exceed the\nexpectations we had for our heroes, we Agarthans.
MID_EV30_009_m01_063: Yes, that is what draws me to you. That is\nit precisely.
MID_EV30_009_m01_064: This passing of traits through blood could be seen\nas another form of causality.
MID_EV30_009_m01_065: The curse you speak of is rooted in karma, to be sure.
MID_EV30_009_m01_066: But 'tis rather ironic to think that the curse now\ndrives you to take up arms against Balor.
MID_EV30_009_m01_067: But let's waste no more time brooding! A vital task\nstill lies before us.
MID_EV30_009_m01_068: There is a troublesome gate that wants destroying.